Current bug report: {'summary': 'TarArchiveOutputStream.getBytesWritten() returns invalid value', 'description': "It appears the TarArchiveOutputStream.getBytesWritten()returns zero or invalid value when queried.  \nIn the code sample below, it returns zero, even after an sizeable file was processed.  \nI've printed it twice, once before closing the output stream, and once after, just for the reference.  \nIt is also demonstrable on multiple processed files.\nWithin the TarArchiveOutputStream.getBytesWritten() im"}

